+# Installing CrashSentinel
+
+<!-- #ju56Us -->
+
+CrashSentinel is a Qt/C++ Linux crash-monitoring and recovery-analysis project.
+
+## Flatpak / Flathub
+
+When the public Flathub listing is available:
+
+```bash
+flatpak install flathub org.oneal.CrashSentinel
+flatpak run org.oneal.CrashSentinel
+```
+
+The Flatpak package is primarily the GUI/report-viewer distribution. A sandboxed
+Flatpak should not be assumed to provide unrestricted host-level monitoring.
+
+## Snap
+
+When a stable Snap Store release is publicly available:
+
+```bash
+sudo snap install crashsentinel
+```
+
+A locally built Snap can be installed for testing with:
+
+```bash
+sudo snap install ./crashsentinel_0.1.0_amd64.snap --dangerous
+```
+
+The Snap packaging includes the GUI and the system-monitor service. Store
+availability can be checked with:
+
+```bash
+snap info crashsentinel
+```
+
+## Build from source
+
+The project requires CMake and Qt 6 components Widgets and Network.
+
+```bash
+cmake -S . -B build
+cmake --build build -j2
+```
+
+The exact executable location depends on the selected CMake generator/build
+directory.
+
